      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As far as I'm aware, dynamic bones scale horribly mathematically. Every single dynamic bone will have to check if it's within the bounds of every single dynamic bone collider. This means that 10 avatars capable of interacting with eachother will likely run 100 times slower (I can't be bothered to do the math, but it's something like that)\nYou could get around this by only considering avatars within 2 meters of yourself or something, I'm not sure how the modded clients have handled it.\nThe rest are similar.. They will need to be implimented in a way which doesn't cause extra load for VRChat's servers or users in general. If modded clients have done something *smart*, then sure, VRChat could learn from it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
