  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-09-19T06:10:15.221Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So, if bans are going to happen because of other's using EMM/melonloader and the like. Why not implement some of the functionality of EMM that users really liked? Namely, interacting with other's dynamic bones, more favorites, editing UI color, and avatar searching. Now let me explain why these are good. Global bone interaction adds to the immersion of the game. And WHY EVEN ALLOW THEM IF YOU CAN'T INTERACT WITH THEM. It's weird having them if you can't do anything with them? May as well ban NSFW users too at that rate. More favorites is a no brainer. I don't know how it would be implemented but honestly, 16? There are a LOT of community avatars that people like, and you limit sharing of those with only 16 favorites. Maybe even add a favorites tiers depending on user levels or systems specs. Editing UI color is just a nice visual thing. Not sure why it's not standard. And as for searching avatars.. why not? It helps on cache weight as you don't have to load numerous worlds searching for avatars. Worlds would still get plenty of visits even with avatar searching. And no I am not being hateful or mean or overly critical. Just.. work with people to improve the overall game? Reach out to the mod creators and ask for help? Please, just consider it.",
